<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Pharmacodynamics & Drug-Receptor Interactions - Master Guide</title>
    <!-- Google Fonts & FontAwesome -->
    <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Inter:wght@300;400;500;600;700&family=Fira+Code:wght@400;500&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/font-awesome/6.4.0/css/all.min.css">
    
    <style>
        :root {
            --primary: #4f46e5;
            --primary-dark: #3730a3;
            --secondary: #06b6d4;
            --accent: #f59e0b;
            --highlight: #fef08a;
            --bg-color: #f8fafc;
            --card-bg: #ffffff;
            --text-main: #1e293b;
            --text-muted: #64748b;
            --border: #e2e8f0;
            --sidebar-width: 280px;
            --transition: all 0.3s ease;
        }

        [data-theme="dark"] {
            --bg-color: #0f172a;
            --card-bg: #1e293b;
            --text-main: #f1f5f9;
            --text-muted: #94a3b8;
            --border: #334155;
            --highlight: #854d0e;
        }

        * {
            box-sizing: border-box;
            margin: 0;
            padding: 0;
            scroll-behavior: smooth;
        }

        body {
            font-family: 'Inter', sans-serif;
            background-color: var(--bg-color);
            color: var(--text-main);
            line-height: 1.6;
            display: flex;
            min-height: 100vh;
        }

        /* Highlight Style for Important/Exam Content */
        mark, .exam-highlight {
            background-color: var(--highlight);
            color: var(--text-main);
            padding: 0.1em 0.3em;
            border-radius: 4px;
            font-weight: 500;
        }

        /* Sidebar Navigation for PC */
        sidebar {
            width: var(--sidebar-width);
            background: var(--card-bg);
            border-right: 1px solid var(--border);
            position: fixed;
            height: 100vh;
            overflow-y: auto;
            transition: var(--transition);
            z-index: 100;
        }

        .sidebar-header {
            padding: 20px;
            border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
            display: flex;
            align-items: center;
            justify-content: space-between;
        }

        .sidebar-header h2 {
            font-size: 1.1rem;
            color: var(--primary);
        }

        .nav-links {
            list-style: none;
            padding: 20px 10px;
        }

        .nav-links li {
            margin-bottom: 8px;
        }

        .nav-links a {
            display: flex;
            align-items: center;
            gap: 10px;
            padding: 10px 15px;
            color: var(--text-muted);
            text-decoration: none;
            border-radius: 8px;
            font-size: 0.9rem;
            transition: var(--transition);
        }

        .nav-links a:hover, .nav-links a.active {
            background: var(--primary);
            color: white;
        }

        /* Main Content Layout */
        main {
            flex: 1;
            margin-left: var(--sidebar-width);
            padding: 40px;
            max-width: 1200px;
            transition: var(--transition);
        }

        /* Top Bar & Theme Toggle */
        .top-bar {
            display: flex;
            justify-content: space-between;
            align-items: center;
            margin-bottom: 30px;
            background: var(--card-bg);
            padding: 15px 25px;
            border-radius: 12px;
            border: 1px solid var(--border);
        }

        .theme-toggle, .menu-toggle {
            background: none;
            border: 1px solid var(--border);
            color: var(--text-main);
            padding: 8px 12px;
            border-radius: 8px;
            cursor: pointer;
            transition: var(--transition);
        }

        .menu-toggle {
            display: none;
        }

        /* Sections & Cards */
        section {
            background: var(--card-bg);
            border: 1px solid var(--border);
            border-radius: 16px;
            padding: 30px;
            margin-bottom: 30px;
            box-shadow: 0 4px 6px -1px rgba(0,0,0,0.05);
            animation: fadeIn 0.6s ease-in-out;
        }

        @keyframes fadeIn {
            from { opacity: 0; transform: translateY(15px); }
            to { opacity: 1; transform: translateY(0); }
        }

        h1 {
            font-size: 2.2rem;
            margin-bottom: 15px;
            background: linear-gradient(135deg, var(--primary), var(--secondary));
            -webkit-background-clip: text;
            -webkit-text-fill-color: transparent;
        }

        h2 {
            font-size: 1.5rem;
            margin-bottom: 20px;
            padding-bottom: 10px;
            border-bottom: 2px solid var(--border);
            color: var(--primary);
            display: flex;
            align-items: center;
            gap: 10px;
        }

        h3 {
            font-size: 1.1rem;
            margin: 20px 0 10px 0;
            color: var(--secondary);
        }

        p, li {
            margin-bottom: 12px;
            color: var(--text-muted);
            font-size: 0.95rem;
        }

        ul {
            padding-left: 20px;
        }

        /* Grid Layout for Receptors */
        .grid-4 {
            display: grid;
            grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(240px, 1fr));
            gap: 20px;
            margin-top: 20px;
        }

        .receptor-card {
            background: var(--bg-color);
            border: 1px solid var(--border);
            border-radius: 12px;
            padding: 20px;
            transition: var(--transition);
            position: relative;
            overflow: hidden;
        }

        .receptor-card:hover {
            transform: translateY(-5px);
            border-color: var(--primary);
            box-shadow: 0 10px 15px -3px rgba(0,0,0,0.1);
        }

        .receptor-card i {
            font-size: 1.8rem;
            color: var(--primary);
            margin-bottom: 15px;
        }

        /* Interactive Graph Simulator */
        .sim-container {
            background: var(--bg-color);
            border: 1px solid var(--border);
            border-radius: 12px;
            padding: 20px;
            margin-top: 20px;
        }

        .canvas-wrapper {
            position: relative;
            width: 100%;
            height: 300px;
            background: var(--card-bg);
            border-radius: 8px;
            border: 1px solid var(--border);
            display: flex;
            align-items: center;
            justify-content: center;
            overflow: hidden;
        }

        .sim-controls {
            display: flex;
            gap: 10px;
            margin-top: 15px;
            flex-wrap: wrap;
        }

        .btn {
            background: var(--primary);
            color: white;
            border: none;
            padding: 8px 16px;
            border-radius: 6px;
            cursor: pointer;
            font-weight: 500;
            transition: var(--transition);
        }

        .btn:hover {
            background: var(--primary-dark);
        }

        /* Responsive Design */
        @media (max-width: 968px) {
            sidebar {
                transform: translateX(-100%);
            }
            sidebar.active {
                transform: translateX(0);
            }
            main {
                margin-left: 0;
                padding: 20px;
            }
            .menu-toggle {
                display: block;
            }
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body data-theme="light">

    <!-- Sidebar Navigation -->
    <sidebar id="sidebar">
        <div class="sidebar-header">
            <h2><i class="fa-solid fa-capsules"></i> Pharmacodynamics</h2>
        </div>
        <ul class="nav-links">
            <li><a href="#intro" class="active"><i class="fa-solid fa-home"></i> Introduction</a></li>
            <li><a href="#receptors"><i class="fa-solid fa-network-wired"></i> Receptor Families</a></li>
            <li><a href="#doseresponse"><i class="fa-solid fa-chart-line"></i> Dose-Response</a></li>
            <li><a href="#agonists"><i class="fa-solid fa-bolt"></i> Agonists & Types</a></li>
            <li><a href="#antagonists"><i class="fa-solid fa-shield-halved"></i> Antagonists</a></li>
        </ul>
    </sidebar>

    <!-- Main Content Area -->
    <main>
        <div class="top-bar">
            <button class="menu-toggle" id="menuToggle"><i class="fa-solid fa-bars"></i></button>
            <span style="font-weight: 600; color: var(--text-muted);">High-Yield Pharmacology Study Suite</span>
            <button class="theme-toggle" id="themeToggle"><i class="fa-solid fa-moon"></i></button>
        </div>

        <!-- Section 1: Introduction -->
        <section id="intro">
            <h1>Pharmacodynamics & Drug-Receptors</h1>
            <p><strong>Pharmacodynamics</strong> describes the actions of a drug on the body and the influence of drug concentrations on the magnitude of the response. Most drugs exert their effects by interacting with specialized target macromolecules called <mark>receptors</mark> present on the cell surface or within the cell.</p>
            
            <h3>Key Concepts & Exceptions</h3>
            <ul>
                <li><strong>Signal Transduction:</strong> The drug–receptor complex initiates biochemical/molecular alterations.</li>
                <li><strong>Receptor Nature:</strong> Most targets are <em>protein molecules</em> (even general anesthetics interact with membrane proteins).</li>
                <li><mark>High-Yield Exam Exception:</mark> Antimicrobial, antitumor, mutagenic, and carcinogenic agents interact <strong>directly with DNA</strong> rather than proteins.</li>
            </ul>
        </section>

        <!-- Section 2: Types of Receptors -->
        <section id="receptors">
            <h2><i class="fa-solid fa-network-wired"></i> The Four Receptor Families</h2>
            <p>Receptors transduce extracellular signals into intracellular responses. Their localization depends on the chemical nature of the ligand: <mark>Hydrophilic ligands</mark> bind cell-surface receptors, whereas <mark>hydrophobic ligands</mark> cross lipid bilayers to reach intracellular receptors.</p>
            
            <div class="grid-4">
                <div class="receptor-card">
                    <i class="fa-solid fa-bolt"></i>
                    <h3>1. Ligand-Gated Ion Channels</h3>
                    <p>Regulate ion pore shape. Activation opens channels briefly (milliseconds).<br><mark>Exam Example:</mark> Nicotinic (Na+ influx) & GABA (Cl- influx).</p>
                </div>
                <div class="receptor-card">
                    <i class="fa-solid fa-circle-nodes"></i>
                    <h3>2. G Protein-Coupled (GPCRs)</h3>
                    <p>Composed of $\alpha, \beta, \gamma$ subunits. $\alpha$-subunit binds GTP, releasing Gs/Gi/Gq second messengers (cAMP, IP3, DAG).</p>
                </div>
                <div class="receptor-card">
                    <i class="fa-solid fa-microchip"></i>
                    <h3>3. Enzyme-Linked Receptors</h3>
                    <p>Form dimers with intrinsic enzymatic activity (mostly tyrosine kinase). <br><mark>Exam Example:</mark> Insulin receptor auto-phosphorylation.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="receptor-card">
                    <i class="fa-solid fa-dna"></i>
                    <h3>4. Intracellular Receptors</h3>
                    <p>Entirely internal; ligands must be lipid-soluble. Targets transcription factors in the nucleus.<br><mark>Exam Example:</mark> Steroid hormones.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>

        <!-- Section 3: Dose-Response Relationship -->
        <section id="doseresponse">
            <h2><i class="fa-solid fa-chart-line"></i> Dose-Response Relationship</h2>
            <p>Binding and activation are distinct steps. <mark>Affinity</mark> governs binding tendency, while <mark>efficacy</mark> governs activation capacity once bound.</p>
            
            <ul>
                <li><strong>Potency:</strong> Amount of drug needed to produce an effect of given magnitude. Measured via <mark>EC50</mark> (drug dose causing 50% maximal response). Lower EC50 = Higher Potency.</li>
                <li><strong>Efficacy ($E_{max}$):</strong> Magnitude of response caused by a drug. <mark>Clinically more useful</mark> than potency!</li>
                <li><strong>Spare Receptors:</strong> Systems possessing a receptor reserve where maximal responses occur at very low occupancies (e.g., &lt;1%).</li>
            </ul>

            <!-- Interactive Simulation Box -->
            <div class="sim-container">
                <h3>Interactive Graded Dose-Response Curve Simulator</h3>
                <p>Visualize how semi-logarithmic transformation converts rectangular hyperbolas into sigmoidal curves.</p>
                <div class="canvas-wrapper">
                    <svg id="curveSvg" width="100%" height="100%" viewBox="0 0 500 250">
                        <!-- Grid lines -->
                        <line x1="50" y1="200" x2="450" y2="200" stroke="var(--border)" stroke-width="2"/>
                        <line x1="50" y1="30" x2="50" y2="200" stroke="var(--border)" stroke-width="2"/>
                        <!-- Sigmoidal Curve Simulation -->
                        <path id="simPath" d="M 50 195 Q 200 195 250 115 T 450 35" fill="none" stroke="var(--primary)" stroke-width="3"/>
                        <text x="230" y="230" fill="var(--text-muted)" font-size="12">Log Concentration (Dose)</text>
                        <text x="10" y="120" fill="var(--text-muted)" font-size="12" transform="rotate(-90 10 120)">Response (%)</text>
                    </svg>
                </div>
                <div class="sim-controls">
                    <button class="btn" onclick="updateCurve('high')">High Potency (Left Shift)</button>
                    <button class="btn" onclick="updateCurve('low')">Low Potency (Right Shift)</button>
                    <button class="btn" onclick="updateCurve('normal')">Reset Curve</button>
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>

        <!-- Section 4: Agonists -->
        <section id="agonists">
            <h2><i class="fa-solid fa-bolt"></i> Agonist Categories</h2>
            <div class="grid-4">
                <div class="receptor-card">
                    <h3>Full Agonists</h3>
                    <p>Intrinsic activity = 1. Mimics endogenous ligand completely, stabilizing active receptor state ($R^*$).<br><mark>Example:</mark> Phenylephrine ($\alpha_1$).</p>
                </div>
                <div class="receptor-card">
                    <h3>Partial Agonists</h3>
                    <p>Intrinsic activity &gt; 0 and &lt; 1. Cannot produce maximal $E_{max}$ even at 100% occupancy. <br><mark>Exam Note:</mark> Can act as an antagonist in the presence of full agonists!</p>
                </div>
                <div class="receptor-card">
                    <h3>Inverse Agonists</h3>
                    <p>Intrinsic activity &lt; 0. Stabilizes inactive form ($R$) and decreases constitutive receptor activity below basal levels.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>

        <!-- Section 5: Antagonists -->
        <section id="antagonists">
            <h2><i class="fa-solid fa-shield-halved"></i> Antagonist Mechanisms</h2>
            <p>Antagonists bind receptors with high affinity but possess <mark>zero intrinsic activity</mark>.</p>
            <ul>
                <li><strong>Competitive Antagonism:</strong> Progressively inhibits response; can be <em>surmounted</em> by increasing agonist concentration. Shifts log concentration curve to the <strong>right</strong> (increases apparent $EC_{50}$) without changing $E_{max}$.</li>
                <li><strong>Noncompetitive Antagonism:</strong> Binds irreversibly (often covalently) or binds allosterically. Agonists <strong>cannot surmount</strong> the inhibitory effect at high concentrations ($E_{max}$ decreases).</li>
                <li><strong>Allosteric Modulators:</strong> Bind separate sites. Negative modulators decrease response; <mark>Positive modulators</mark> (e.g., Benzodiazepines on GABA) enhance activation.</li>
                <li><strong>Functional / Physiological Antagonism:</strong> Acts at a completely separate receptor to produce opposing effects (e.g., Epinephrine vs. Histamine on bronchial smooth muscle).</li>
            </ul>
        </section>
    </main>

    <!-- Script Interactions -->
    <script>
        // Theme Switcher Logic
        const themeToggle = document.getElementById('themeToggle');
        const body = document.body;
        themeToggle.addEventListener('click', () => {
            if(body.getAttribute('data-theme') === 'light') {
                body.setAttribute('data-theme', 'dark');
                themeToggle.innerHTML = '<i class="fa-solid fa-sun"></i>';
            } else {
                body.setAttribute('data-theme', 'light');
                themeToggle.innerHTML = '<i class="fa-solid fa-moon"></i>';
            }
        });

        // Mobile Sidebar Toggle
        const menuToggle = document.getElementById('menuToggle');
        const sidebar = document.getElementById('sidebar');
        menuToggle.addEventListener('click', () => {
            sidebar.classList.toggle('active');
        });

        // Interactive Graph Simulation Script
        function updateCurve(type) {
            const path = document.getElementById('simPath');
            if(type === 'high') {
                path.setAttribute('d', 'M 50 195 Q 120 195 150 115 T 350 35');
            } else if(type === 'low') {
                path.setAttribute('d', 'M 50 195 Q 300 195 350 115 T 450 35');
            } else {
                path.setAttribute('d', 'M 50 195 Q 200 195 250 115 T 450 35');
            }
        }
    </script>
</body>
</html>
